.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-relocate 1  "rev-stealth-relocate " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-relocate \- Locate a previously fingerprinted element in a saved HTML or fresh URL
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth relocate\fR [\fB\-\-output\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-session\-id\fR] <\fB\-\-stable\-id\fR> [\fB\-\-html\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-parse\-store\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-\-i\-have\-authorization\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-no\-vpn\fR] [\fB\-\-vpn\-instance\fR] [\fB\-\-proxy\-tier\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-\-use\-auth\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-domain\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Locate a previously fingerprinted element by stable_id against either a local HTML file (\-\-html\-file) or a fresh fetch (\-\-url, HTTP\-only). Returns the best CSS selector + similarity score from ParseStore.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-format\fR \fI<OUTPUT_FORMAT>\fR
Output format for this subcommand: `human` (default) or `json`. Shadows the global `\-\-format` for this invocation. Same value enum as the global flag; the JSON output is documented under `docs/json\-schemas/cli/<subcommand>.output.json`
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-session\-id\fR \fI<SESSION_ID>\fR
Session id (informational; not required to open the store)
.TP
\fB\-\-stable\-id\fR \fI<STABLE_ID>\fR
stable_id of the element to locate
.TP
\fB\-\-html\-file\fR \fI<HTML_FILE>\fR
Local HTML file to scan
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Remote URL to fetch (HTTP\-only, no browser launch)
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0.85]
Similarity threshold
.TP
\fB\-\-parse\-store\fR \fI<PARSE_STORE>\fR
Optional ParseStore path (defaults to `~/.rev_scraping/parse.sqlite`)
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Treat Ambiguous as exit 10
.TP
\fB\-\-i\-have\-authorization\fR
AUP bypass (logs a warn). Required when `\-\-url` targets a non\-allowlisted host
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-vpn\fR
Phase 6c: fail\-closed VPN\-required guard. Applies to `\-\-url` only; `\-\-html\-file` is a local read
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-no\-vpn\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-vpn\-instance\fR \fI<VPN_INSTANCE>\fR
Phase 6d: force a specific VPN instance from the configured pool
.TP
\fB\-\-proxy\-tier\fR \fI<PROXY_TIER>\fR
Force a named proxy tier (e.g. "direct", "surfshark", "warp", "iproyal") or "auto" to use the configured fallback chain. Mutually exclusive with `\-\-vpn\-instance` unless the tier is exactly "surfshark"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-fallback\fR
Disable the fallback chain; one attempt at the selected tier only
.TP
\fB\-\-use\-auth\fR \fI<USE_AUTH>\fR
Replay stored auth cookies and browser headers from the named profile
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-domain\fR \fI<AUTH_DOMAIN>\fR
Auth AAD/domain context to load; defaults to the target host
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth relocate \-\-stable\-id abc123 \-\-html\-file saved.html
  $ rev\-stealth relocate \-\-stable\-id abc123 \-\-url https://example.com \-\-i\-have\-authorization
  $ rev\-stealth relocate \-\-stable\-id abc123 \-\-html\-file saved.html \-\-strict \-\-threshold 0.9

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Match found above threshold.
  1  UserError        Bad args / AUP rejection / missing stable_id.
  3  PermanentError   ParseStore open failure or no candidate found.

ENV:
  REV_SCRAPING_HOME  Override `~/.rev_scraping/` (ParseStore location).
